### Tested versions

Latest master as of writing 741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9

### System information

macOS 15.7 arm64

### Issue description

When using Godot to perform a runtime import of glTF files, this will succeed if importing a regular file without physics. If you put this on a thread, it still works. If you import a file with a physics object with a mesh-based shape not on a thread, then it works. However, if you try to import this on a thread, Godot will hang forever, not printing any error messages. Godot seems to be able to import very simple physics objects on a thread, like a cube with a box shape, but it hangs for mesh-based shapes.

### Steps to reproduce

Open the minimal reproduction project and run it. This will work:

<img width="586" height="431" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c78bfcc8-2488-46e1-94c0-ae4cd468438f" />

Then, change this line of code to true:

```
var use_thread: bool = false
```

If you run again, Godot will hang, never drawing a single frame:

<img width="586" height="431" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef4ce2c5-f454-46c5-84d4-5471a1a3a5e9" />

Here is the test code placed on the root node of the MRP scene:

<details>

```gdscript
extends Node


var root_nodes: Array[Node] = []
var root_nodes_mutex := Mutex.new()
var use_thread: bool = true


func _ready() -> void:
	var threads: Array[Thread] = []
	var path: String = ProjectSettings.globalize_path("res://noeditorimport")
	var dir = DirAccess.open(path)
	dir.list_dir_begin()
	var filename: String = dir.get_next()
	while not filename.is_empty():
		var file_path: String = path.path_join(filename)
		if use_thread:
			var thread := Thread.new()
			thread.start(_import_glb.bind(file_path))
			threads.append(thread)
		else:
			_import_glb(file_path)
		filename = dir.get_next()
	for thread in threads:
		thread.wait_to_finish()
	for root_node in root_nodes:
		add_child(root_node)


func _import_glb(file_path: String) -> void:
	var doc := GLTFDocument.new()
	var state := GLTFState.new()
	var err = doc.append_from_file(file_path, state)
	if err != OK:
		printerr("Error importing glTF: Error " + str(err))
		return
	var root_node: Node = doc.generate_scene(state)
	if root_node == null:
		printerr("Error importing glTF: Root node was null.")
		return
	root_nodes_mutex.lock()
	root_nodes.append(root_node)
	root_nodes_mutex.unlock()
```

</details>

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[threaded-gltf-import-hang.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24692558/threaded-gltf-import-hang.zip)
